## Client-Facing PDPA Response (send as-is)

> **Subject: Your Personal Data Request — Winfred Quek | CEA R073319H | PropNex**

Dear [Name],

Thank you for reaching out. I take data privacy seriously and am happy to address your request under Singapore's Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (PDPA).

**What personal data I may hold about you**
Depending on how we've interacted: name, contact details (phone/email), nationality, financial profile (income range, CPF balances, loan pre-approval), property portfolio details you've shared, correspondence from WhatsApp/Telegram/email/calls, property offers or transactions I've assisted with, and Calendly booking records.

**Where it is stored**
Secure cloud-hosted database (Neon Postgres), my business Gmail, WhatsApp Business and Telegram bot logs (processed via n8n), and Calendly. If you enquired via PropertyGuru or 99.co, those platforms also hold a copy under their own privacy policies.

**How to request access, correction, or erasure**
Email **winfredquekoc@gmail.com** with subject line: *"PDPA Request — [Your Name]"* — specify whether you want (a) access, (b) correction, or (c) erasure/consent withdrawal. I'll acknowledge within 3 business days and respond fully within **30 business days** as required by PDPA.

**Exemptions**
Completed transaction records (OTP, SPA, commission) must be retained under CEA regulatory rules even after consent withdrawal. I'll identify any such records clearly when responding.

Warm regards,
Winfred Quek | CEA R073319H | PropNex Realty Pte Ltd

